# Akaion Runner — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env (or .env.prod / .env.dev for use with start.sh's RUNNER_ENV
# loader). Lines prefixed with `#` are comments / examples.

# ── Backend resolver ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The runner talks to three backends behind a single host:
#   main → {AKAION_API_BASE}/api/service1   (auth, identity)
#   cot  → {AKAION_API_BASE}/api/service3   (Brain push)
#   ai   → {AKAION_API_BASE}/api/service4   (optional cloud LLM)
#
# In production set AKAION_API_BASE to your Akaion-compatible host.
# In development point each service at localhost (see overrides below).

ENVIRONMENT=production
AKAION_API_BASE=https://api.akaion.com

# Development override — comment AKAION_API_BASE above and uncomment these:
#   ENVIRONMENT=development
#   # ports default to: main=8080, cot=8083, ai=8084

# ── Per-service override (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these only if a service lives on a different host (e.g. staging).
# AKAION_MAIN_URL=https://api.akaion.com/api/service1
# AKAION_COT_URL=https://api.akaion.com/api/service3
# AKAION_AI_URL=https://api.akaion.com/api/service4

# ── Profile isolation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, the runner stores its config / auth / vault under this directory
# instead of ~/.akaion. Useful when running multiple installs (source + .dmg)
# on the same machine.
# AKAION_HOME=$HOME/.akaion

# ── Firebase web API key (public) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Web SDK API keys are designed to be exposed client-side; they are
# NOT secrets. Override only if you point the runner at a different Firebase
# project than the default Akaion one.
# FIREBASE_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: AI inference keys (used only if the cloud AI backend is OFF) ───
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ── Knobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AKAION_DEV_MODE=false
AKAION_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Capture every executed task as a local Brain note (default: true).
# AKAION_CAPTURE_TO_BRAIN=1

# Brain vault path (default: ~/akaion-brain).
# AKAION_BRAIN_DIR=$HOME/akaion-brain

# ── Cloud sync (opt-in) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The runner is local-first: cloud.enabled=false by default in
# ~/.akaion/config.yaml. Enable persistently with `akaion cloud enable`, or
# force-local for a single run with `akaion run --no-cloud`. Sync is one-way
# (local → remote): the runner pushes notes you mark as `pending`, never pulls.
